window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-1343b65da02838d5"]={"key":"ny_b1-1343b65da02838d5","group":"ny_b1","uid":"1343b65da02838d5","rank":32,"title":"saltmarsh discovery engagement proposal","occupation":"computer_information_systems_managers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Lorcan Egwuatu, a computer and information systems manager advising Saltmarsh Growers Co-operative. Karin Abara wants a short pitch for the member-elected technology panel, which meets on 14 October to decide whether to fund Kestrel Lane Advisory for a paid three-month discovery-and-roadmap engagement or continue improvising with the two members who are “good with computers.” The panel has never paid for outside IT help, and its main concern is that consultants leave behind a report while nothing actually works afterwards. Prepare `saltmarsh_discovery_proposal.docx` and `saltmarsh_roadmap.xlsx` in the top level of the working directory, using exactly those filenames. The Word file is the pitch the panel will read once without you present: keep it to two pages, write for non-specialists, make one clear recommendation, and explain what the engagement will and will not deliver. Include enough commercial and delivery information for the panel to judge whether the spend is sensible, but do not pretend that a working system, procurement decision, or guaranteed savings will exist at the end of three months. The spreadsheet is the supporting phased roadmap and must agree with the Word file wherever they share dates, durations, costs, decisions, owners, or outcomes. Show the work as a practical sequence from mobilisation through discovery, prioritisation, and handover, with visible decision points and a useful account of what happens if a planned interview, access request, or discovery activity cannot be completed. Make the material understandable to people who are not IT professionals, including readers familiar with organisations such as Bramblewood Clinic and Overbrook Council, and do not assume that the panel knows consulting terminology. Address the fear of dependency directly, including how Saltmarsh will retain knowledge and make decisions after Kestrel Lane Advisory leaves. Do not include software click-by-click instructions, a technical architecture, or a long catalogue of products. Put the final recommendation at the end of the Word document rather than ending with a list of possible next steps.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `saltmarsh_discovery_proposal.docx` — A concise, non-specialist proposal and recommendation for the three-month discovery-and-roadmap engagement. (Exactly two pages when rendered with normal document settings; Must be readable by a technology panel without an author present; Must contain one clear recommendation; Must not include software click-through instructions, technical architecture, or a product catalogue; Must end with the recommendation rather than a further-steps list)\n- `saltmarsh_roadmap.xlsx` — A phased three-month discovery roadmap supporting the proposal, with activities, timing, ownership, decisions, dependencies, outputs, assumptions, and exception handling. (Must be understandable to non-specialists; Must show a coherent three-month sequence and decision points; Must agree with the Word proposal on all shared figures and commitments; Must distinguish planned work from assumptions and unresolved decisions)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/saltmarsh_discovery_proposal.docx","bytes":40901,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/925e5ac778a1a9922423c47afcf4de7437b89e7c194e3cfff47b530a18d2fb32.docx","sha256":"925e5ac778a1a9922423c47afcf4de7437b89e7c194e3cfff47b530a18d2fb32","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"DECISION BRIEFING\nA practical route out of informal technology support\nPrepared by Lorcan Egwuatu, Kestrel Lane Advisory  |  For Karin Abara and the member-elected technology panel  |  14 October decision\nASK\nFund a paid, bounded discovery engagement\nDURATION\n12 weeks from mobilisation to handover\nFEE\n£18,600 fixed fee, excluding VAT and agreed travel\nWhy this decision matters\nSaltmarsh Growers Co-operative has reached the point where goodwill is not enough. Two members who are “good with computers” have kept things moving, but informal fixes can create single-person dependency, inconsistent records and access, lost knowledge, and security exposure. They also make it hard for the panel to compare needs fairly. This engagement replaces improvisation with shared evidence and agreed choices—not a consultant-owned answer.\nIt is deliberately similar in scale to a small service organisation: listen first, make the facts visible, then agree the order of work. It is not a technical design exercise and does not assume the panel needs to know specialist language.\nWhat Kestrel Lane will do in 12 weeks\nWeeks 1–2 — Mobilisation and scope. Confirm the questions, name owners, arrange access and interviews, and agree how gaps will be recorded.\nWeeks 3–6 — Discovery and baseline. Hear from members and volunteers; review day-to-day working practices, information handling, pain points, risks, and current ownership. At the end of Week 6, the technology panel decides whether to accept, revise, defer, or reject the evidence-based priorities.\nWeeks 7–10 — Prioritisation and validation. Order possible improvements by member value, urgency, effort, risk, and confidence in the evidence. Saltmarsh reviews the findings in a working session; Kestrel Lane corrects misunderstandings before drafting the roadmap.\nWeeks 11–12 — Decision package and handover. Complete the roadmap, decision record, and ownership handover. In Week 12, the panel reviews and accepts the discovery outputs.\n\n\nWhat you will receive—and what you will not\nThe end product is a decision-quality plan: an agreed current-state baseline; a clear evidence log showing confidence, assumptions and unanswered questions; a prioritised 12-week-to-longer-term roadmap; risks and dependencies; a decision record; and a handover pack owned by Saltmarsh. The roadmap will make later choices easier, including whether any separate implementation or purchase is worth authorising.\nThis engagement does not deliver a working system, choose a product, run a procurement, or guarantee savings. That boundary is useful: it lets the panel see real needs, costs, risks and ownership before committing to a solution. Findings and recommendations are not approval to buy or implement anything; those remain later Saltmarsh decisions.\nHow Saltmarsh stays in control\nKestrel Lane will work alongside named Saltmarsh owners, not in a black box. Karin Abara sponsors access and decisions; a panel representative confirms priorities; the two volunteer helpers contribute their knowledge but do not make unilateral technology choices. Shared review sessions, plain-language working notes, a maintained decision record and a handover session mean the co-operative keeps the reasoning as well as the files. After handover, the panel can use the roadmap without ongoing advisory dependency.\nSaltmarsh involvement is modest but essential: a 60-minute weekly sponsor check-in, up to eight 45-minute interviews across Weeks 3–5, timely access to relevant records, and two panel reviews (Week 6 and Week 12). The adviser manages the load and will not ask volunteers to build systems during discovery.\nManaging uncertainty and the spend\nThe £18,600 fixed fee (excluding VAT and agreed travel) covers the 12-week engagement and the outputs above. No implementation costs are included. If an interview, record, or access request cannot be completed, Kestrel Lane will log the gap, use an agreed substitute such as a group session or existing record where possible, mark the affected finding as unverified with a confidence level, and bring any material timing or scope effect to Karin and the panel. The panel—not the adviser—decides whether to accept, change, defer, or stop affected work.\nThis is also a safer alternative to shadow systems. Until the panel has considered the evidence, new workarounds, shared accounts, and unreviewed purchases should not be introduced by well-meaning volunteers. Urgent operational issues can be recorded and escalated through Karin for a proportionate panel decision.\nRECOMMENDATION  |  Fund Kestrel Lane Advisory’s £18,600 fixed-fee, 12-week discovery-and-roadmap engagement. It gives Saltmarsh an owned, evidence-tested route to decide what—if anything—to implement next, without committing the co-operative to a working system, product purchase, or continuing consultancy.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/saltmarsh_roadmap.xlsx","bytes":8749,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/45264975c9c7d6ba7ace1d440330996f17846b75e7e08de141aee064af968d95.xlsx","sha256":"45264975c9c7d6ba7ace1d440330996f17846b75e7e08de141aee064af968d95","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"3-month roadmap","row_count":24,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Saltmarsh Growers Co-operative — 12-week discovery & roadmap"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Kestrel Lane Advisory | Fixed fee: £18,600 excluding VAT and agreed travel | No implementation costs included"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Purpose: decision-quality evidence, prioritised roadmap, decision record and handover pack — not a working system, product approval or procurement decision."]},{"r":"4","cells":["Decision context: member-elected technology panel meets 14 October to decide whether to fund the engagement."]},{"r":"6","cells":["Phase","Weeks","Activity","Saltmarsh owner","Kestrel owner","Evidence / output","Depends on","Decision or status","If incomplete / confidence"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Mobilisation","W1","Kick-off: confirm purpose, boundaries, contact list and weekly check-in.","Karin Abara (sponsor)","Lorcan Egwuatu","Agreed scope; contact plan; open evidence log.","Panel funding decision","Start only after scope is agreed.","If scope is unclear, log change and escalate to Karin; panel decides material change."]},{"r":"8","cells":["Mobilisation","W1–2","Arrange interviews and request access to relevant records and existing shared tools.","Karin Abara","Lorcan Egwuatu","Interview schedule; access tracker.","Kick-off; member availability","Planned.","If unavailable, use a group session or existing record; record gap and confidence."]},{"r":"9","cells":["Discovery","W3–5","Member and volunteer interviews: what helps, what gets in the way, desired outcomes and pain points.","Panel representative","Lorcan Egwuatu","Interview themes; needs and pain-points log.","Interview schedule","Evidence gathering.","Missed voice is marked “unverified”; no finding is presented as confirmed without validation."]},{"r":"10","cells":["Discovery","W3–5","Current-state review of working practices, information handling, access, risks and ownership.","Volunteer helpers","Lorcan Egwuatu","Current-state baseline; risk and ownership map.","Access tracker; volunteer knowledge","Evidence gathering.","Missing access: substitute existing records where possible; flag limitation, owner and effect on confidence."]},{"r":"11","cells":["Synthesis","W6","Bring evidence together; separate confirmed findings, assumptions and unresolved questions.","Karin Abara","Lorcan Egwuatu","Baseline + evidence log with confidence ratings.","Interview themes; current-state baseline","Ready for Gate 1.","Open gaps remain assumptions, not findings; panel sees timing/confidence effect."]},{"r":"12","cells":["Decision gate 1","End W6","Review evidence and proposed priority criteria: member value, urgency, effort, risk and confidence.","Technology panel","Lorcan Egwuatu","Approved or revised priority criteria; decision record.","Baseline + evidence log","PANEL: accept, revise, defer or reject priorities.","If evidence is insufficient, defer affected item or request focused follow-up; do not guess."]},{"r":"13","cells":["Prioritisation","W7–8","Score improvement themes against approved criteria and evidence; identify dependencies.","Panel representative","Lorcan Egwuatu","Prioritised options; dependency and risk view.","Gate 1 criteria; evidence log","Draft priorities.","Low-confidence items labelled provisional and carry validation needed."]},{"r":"14","cells":["Roadmap drafting","W9","Turn agreed priorities into a practical sequence, owners, prerequisites and decision points.","Karin Abara","Lorcan Egwuatu","Draft roadmap and ownership outline.","Prioritised options; dependencies","Draft for validation.","Scope change is logged; Karin escalates material timing or cost effect to panel."]},{"r":"15","cells":["Validation","W10","Working session: Saltmarsh checks findings, wording, priorities and what remains unknown.","Technology panel","Lorcan Egwuatu","Validated findings; corrections; unresolved questions.","Draft roadmap; decision record","Panel confirmation, not product approval.","Disputed finding stays open with named owner; roadmap states assumption rather than certainty."]},{"r":"16","cells":["Decision package","W11","Complete the roadmap, risk responses, decision record and next-stage choices.","Karin Abara","Lorcan Egwuatu","Final decision package; handover pack.","Validated findings","Ready for final review.","Any open gap is retained in handover pack with owner and validation route."]},{"r":"17","cells":["Handover","W12","Shared handover session: walk through evidence, priorities, files, owners and how to update the roadmap.","Karin Abara + panel representative","Lorcan Egwuatu","Saltmarsh-owned handover pack; maintained decision record.","Final decision package","Knowledge transfer completed.","If owner absent, reschedule within W12; note any transfer not completed."]},{"r":"18","cells":["Decision gate 2","End W12","Final review and acceptance of discovery outputs; decide whether any separate next-stage work is warranted.","Technology panel","Lorcan Egwuatu","Accepted, revised or deferred discovery outputs.","Handover pack","PANEL: accept, revise, defer or reject. No automatic procurement or implementation approval.","Unresolved items remain explicitly deferred with owner; discovery closes on agreed record."]},{"r":"21","cells":["Assumptions, open questions and active risks"]},{"r":"22","cells":["Type","Item","Potential effect","Owner","Response / decision needed"]},{"r":"23","cells":["Assumption","Relevant records can be shared within W1–2.","Delays reduce confidence in baseline.","Karin Abara","Use available records; log missing evidence; panel decides whether focused follow-up is needed."]},{"r":"24","cells":["Open question","Which working practices require urgent attention?","Priority order may change after validation.","Technology panel","Decide at Gate 1 using member value, urgency, effort, risk and confidence."]},{"r":"25","cells":["Risk","Volunteer dependency or unreviewed workarounds continue during discovery.","Lost knowledge, inconsistent access, shadow IT.","Karin Abara","Record urgent issue; pause new workaround or purchase pending proportionate panel decision."]},{"r":"26","cells":["Risk","Scope expands into implementation.","Time and fee no longer match discovery purpose.","Lorcan Egwuatu","Log change; explain impact; panel accepts, revises, defers or rejects before work changes."]},{"r":"27","cells":["Risk","Named owner cannot attend validation or handover.","Findings may be misunderstood after adviser leaves.","Karin Abara","Nominate delegate or reschedule in W12; record transfer gap and retained ownership."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal identifies Saltmarsh Growers Co-operative as the client and Kestrel Lane Advisory as the proposed adviser.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered Word document","grader_hint":"Check the named organisations in the proposal body, not only metadata."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal identifies the 14 October technology-panel decision context.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered Word document","grader_hint":"Verify that the meeting date and decision audience are visible."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Word proposal is no more than two rendered pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page count","grader_hint":"Render with the document's ordinary page settings and count pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposal is understandable to a broad non-specialist audience without an author present.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered Word document","grader_hint":"Judge jargon, sentence density, unexplained acronyms, and whether a non-IT panel member can follow the decision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal gives one unambiguous recommendation to fund or not fund the discovery engagement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final recommendation in Word document","grader_hint":"Accept only one clear call; conditional alternatives or two equal options do not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The recommendation is placed at the end of the Word document and the document does not finish with a generic next-steps list.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Document ending","grader_hint":"Inspect the final substantive paragraph or callout."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal explicitly states that the engagement produces a plan and not a working system at its end.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope or outcome language in Word document","grader_hint":"Look for a direct limitation, not merely an implication from the timetable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal distinguishes discovery, roadmap creation, and later implementation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Word document","grader_hint":"Confirm that implementation is described as a later decision or phase rather than silently included."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The limitation of not delivering a working system is framed as a reason the discovery output can remain honest and decision-useful rather than buried as a disclaimer.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Word document argument","grader_hint":"Assess whether the concession builds trust and clarifies value."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal explains what the panel will receive at the end of the engagement.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Word document","grader_hint":"Expect concrete outputs such as current-state findings, prioritised roadmap, risks, decisions, and handover material."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap covers a coherent progression from mobilisation through discovery and prioritisation to handover.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap workbook","grader_hint":"Check sequence and dependency logic rather than exact labels."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap spans approximately three months and does not schedule the engagement as an unbounded activity.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Dates or week ranges in workbook and proposal","grader_hint":"Accept a reasonable 12- or 13-week interpretation if consistently stated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Early mobilisation precedes substantive discovery work.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap dependencies","grader_hint":"Check that kickoff, scope confirmation, access, and stakeholder scheduling are not placed after analysis."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Discovery activities produce evidence that is used in later prioritisation rather than appearing as disconnected tasks.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Activity, output, and dependency fields","grader_hint":"Trace at least two discovery outputs into prioritisation or roadmap decisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap includes a current-state view or baseline of the relevant technology and working practices.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap outputs","grader_hint":"A meaningful baseline may cover systems, processes, pain points, risks, and ownership."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap includes stakeholder or user discovery rather than relying only on technical inspection.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap activities","grader_hint":"Look for interviews, workshops, observation, or an equivalent evidence-gathering activity."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap identifies business needs, pain points, or outcomes alongside technology observations.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap activities or outputs","grader_hint":"Do not award for a list of tools alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap includes a prioritisation method using value or impact, urgency, effort, risk, or comparable professional criteria.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap or prioritisation section","grader_hint":"The method need not be named after a particular framework but must support defensible ordering."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Priorities are tied to evidence or stated assumptions rather than presented as unsupported technology preferences.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap rationale fields","grader_hint":"Trace representative priorities to discovery findings, stakeholder needs, or clearly marked assumptions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap identifies dependencies or prerequisites for major workstreams.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap dependency information","grader_hint":"Accept dependencies such as access, data quality, stakeholder availability, governance, or funding."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap identifies a decision point at which Saltmarsh can accept, revise, defer, or reject the proposed priorities.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap decision points","grader_hint":"A decision point must state what is being decided and by whom."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap identifies a final review or sign-off point for the discovery outputs.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap","grader_hint":"Check for a final validation, acceptance, or panel review activity."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap names accountable owners for activities or decisions, including a Saltmarsh-side owner and an adviser-side owner.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap owner fields and proposal","grader_hint":"Roles are acceptable where personal names are not appropriate, but ownership must be concrete."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal explains how knowledge will be retained by Saltmarsh after Kestrel Lane Advisory leaves.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Word document","grader_hint":"Look for maintained artefacts, shared working sessions, owner participation, or handover—not merely a promise to provide a report."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap includes a handover or capability-transfer activity before the engagement ends.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap","grader_hint":"The activity should involve transfer of understanding or ownership, not only file delivery."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal sets expectations for the involvement required from Saltmarsh members or panel representatives.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Word document","grader_hint":"Expect time, access, interviews, decisions, or review commitments stated concretely."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap includes a path for an interview, access request, or discovery activity that cannot be completed as planned.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception or contingency treatment in workbook","grader_hint":"Award only when the fallback is operational, such as recording the gap, using a substitute evidence source, assigning an owner, and escalating its effect on confidence or timing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The incomplete-activity path prevents an unverified assumption from being presented as a confirmed finding.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roadmap exception handling and outputs","grader_hint":"Check for explicit marking of unknowns, confidence, assumptions, or validation requirements."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal describes how material scope, evidence, or timing changes will be surfaced and decided.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Word document","grader_hint":"Look for escalation, change control, or panel decision language with an accountable decision maker."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal actively discourages shadow IT or uncontrolled workarounds by the two members who are good with computers.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Word document","grader_hint":"A mere description of current improvisation is insufficient; the document must state a safer behavioural or governance expectation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal distinguishes discovery findings and recommendations from approval to purchase or implement a product.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Word document","grader_hint":"Check that a roadmap item does not automatically become an authorised procurement or implementation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap records assumptions and unresolved questions that could affect the recommendation or later implementation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook","grader_hint":"Accept a dedicated assumptions or risks treatment or clearly labelled fields within the roadmap."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal identifies material risks of continuing with informal, volunteer-led technology support.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Word document","grader_hint":"Examples may include single-person dependency, inconsistent practices, lost knowledge, security exposure, or inability to prioritise."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal states how discovery findings will be validated with Saltmarsh rather than treated as an adviser-only opinion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Word document","grader_hint":"Look for review workshops, confirmation checkpoints, evidence review, or equivalent validation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The roadmap includes risks, blockers, or dependencies with an owner or response where practical.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook","grader_hint":"A risk list without ownership or response is only partial evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposed sequence is feasible for a small co-operative with limited internal technology capacity.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Both deliverables","grader_hint":"Judge whether the plan demands unrealistic parallel work, excessive governance, or specialist participation without acknowledging constraints."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposal explains how the engagement creates value even though it does not itself implement a system.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Word document","grader_hint":"Expect decision-quality evidence, prioritisation, reduced uncertainty, ownership, and an actionable sequence rather than vague transformation claims."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Word proposal and workbook use the same stated engagement duration, phase timing, and major milestone dates.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-document comparison","grader_hint":"Extract every shared timing claim and verify exact agreement or clearly equivalent week/date representations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Word proposal and workbook agree on the engagement fee, budget basis, or other shared commercial figures.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-document comparison","grader_hint":"If figures are expressed as assumptions or estimates, verify that labels and values match in both files."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Word proposal and workbook agree on the major outputs and decision gates they share.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-document comparison","grader_hint":"Compare phase names, deliverables, and decision points; do not require identical wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Both required files exist at the top level with exactly the requested filenames and readable file structures.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Filesystem and file parsing","grader_hint":"Check exact case-sensitive names, extensions, and successful opening."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Taken together, the proposal and roadmap give the panel enough clarity to make a funding decision without asking the author to explain what happens, what is excluded, who participates, or what happens when evidence is missing.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Both rendered deliverables","grader_hint":"Assess practical usability as a decision packet, including coherence, restraint, readable sequencing, and treatment of uncertainty."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"A technology manager is preparing a plain-language investment proposal for a small co-operative whose volunteer technology arrangements have become difficult to govern. The work requires a bounded recommendation, a credible discovery plan, and a usable roadmap rather than a technical implementation design.","difficulty_sources":["Selecting a credible three-month discovery sequence without being given a methodology","Explaining the limits of a discovery engagement while making the recommendation persuasive","Designing a roadmap that a non-specialist panel can understand and act on","Providing a safe path when discovery work cannot be completed","Preventing the common misuse of treating a roadmap as an implementation or approval to buy technology","Keeping assumptions, costs, timing, ownership, and decision points consistent across two deliverables"],"authoring_plan":{"purpose":"Create a realistic two-file proposal package from occupational knowledge, with the Word document functioning as the persuasive briefing and the workbook functioning as the operational roadmap.","document_design":{"proposal":{"content_constraints":["Use Saltmarsh Growers Co-operative and Kestrel Lane Advisory as the central organisations.","Use the 14 October panel meeting as the decision context.","Make a single recommendation to fund the three-month discovery engagement.","State plainly that discovery delivers evidence, priorities, decisions, and a roadmap, not a working system.","Address consultant dependency through shared ownership, working sessions, documented decisions, and handover.","Include a credible commercial assumption and ensure the same value appears in the workbook.","Explain current-state discovery, stakeholder engagement, prioritisation, validation, and handover in concise prose.","Include an explicit exception path for unavailable people, inaccessible information, or incomplete discovery.","Discourage informal shadow systems and unilateral technology choices by technically confident volunteers.","End with the recommendation itself, not with generic next steps."],"figures":"Choose a plausible fixed or capped fee and a consistent three-month timing model. Mark invented commercial values as estimates or assumptions; do not present unsupported savings, implementation costs, or guaranteed outcomes as facts.","names":"Use Karin Abara as the commissioning voice or named sponsor. Use the other supplied personal names only where useful as roles; do not invent additional people."},"roadmap":{"content_constraints":["Represent a coherent sequence: mobilisation and scope, evidence gathering, current-state synthesis, prioritisation, validation, roadmap and decision package, then handover.","Give each major activity a time range, owner, output, dependency or prerequisite where relevant, and decision or status treatment.","Include a decision gate after evidence synthesis and another at final acceptance.","Include a practical exception row or mechanism covering failed interviews, missing access, unavailable records, or incomplete evidence.","Mark uncertainty and confidence so that gaps do not become false findings.","Include risks and responses, especially volunteer dependency, access delays, scope drift, and loss of knowledge.","Use plain-language labels suitable for a broad audience.","Repeat the proposal's fee, duration, phases, major outputs, and decision gates exactly or in clearly equivalent terms."],"commercial_logic":"The workbook may calculate or display totals, but no numeric gold value is required. Its commercial figures must reconcile internally and match the proposal.","professional_expectations":["A roadmap is not an implementation schedule unless implementation has been separately authorised.","Dependencies should affect timing or confidence rather than being decorative text.","Owners must be capable of taking the stated action, with Saltmarsh ownership visible alongside adviser ownership.","The fallback path should identify a substitute evidence source or escalation, record the gap, and show its consequence."]}},"quality_checks":["Render the Word document and verify the two-page maximum.","Open and inspect the workbook formulas or values offline.","Extract shared dates, durations, milestones, fee figures, outputs, and decision gates from both files and compare them.","Check that the proposal does not claim a working system, guaranteed savings, or automatic product approval.","Check that the exception path is actionable and that the shadow-IT misuse is actively discouraged.","Review the final pages and workbook views as a non-specialist panel member."]},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"primary_plus_appendix","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"proposal_docx","filename":"saltmarsh_discovery_proposal.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise, non-specialist proposal and recommendation for the three-month discovery-and-roadmap engagement.","required":true,"constraints":["Exactly two pages when rendered with normal document settings","Must be readable by a technology panel without an author present","Must contain one clear recommendation","Must not include software click-through instructions, technical architecture, or a product catalogue","Must end with the recommendation rather than a further-steps list"],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"roadmap_xlsx","filename":"saltmarsh_roadmap.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"A phased three-month discovery roadmap supporting the proposal, with activities, timing, ownership, decisions, dependencies, outputs, assumptions, and exception handling.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be understandable to non-specialists","Must show a coherent three-month sequence and decision points","Must agree with the Word proposal on all shared figures and commitments","Must distinguish planned work from assumptions and unresolved decisions"],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"make_decisions","work_product":"project_plan","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"computer_information_systems_managers","sector":"professional_scientific_technical_services","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have an independent reviewer inspect the rendered Word proposal and workbook together, verify all cross-deliverable figures and milestones, and judge non-specialist usability. A second reviewer should spot-check the exception path, dependency logic, and the explicit boundary between discovery and implementation.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["Because no supplied commercial rate card exists, the gold should judge consistency, explicit assumptions, and commercial plausibility rather than one required fee.","Professional judgement is required for readability and feasibility; literal phrase matching should not be used for those items."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:16:06+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:16:06+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:16:06+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:16:06+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R30']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:16:06+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/1343b65da02838d5","declared_deliverables":["saltmarsh_discovery_proposal.docx","saltmarsh_roadmap.xlsx"]};
